ection>\n\n            <section class=\"column\">\n                <div class=\"column-header\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n                    No whitelist updates for this period. Existing products continue to evolve with incremental improvements.\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <section class=\"column\">\n                <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://alexispurslane.github.io/rsync-analysis/\">Did Claude increase bugs in rsync?</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Analysis of whether AI-generated code contributions increase bug rates, using rsync as a case study for AI code quality assessment.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Alexis Purslane</a> | 2026-06-05\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Coding</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Code Quality</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review\">Open Code Review - AI-powered CLI tool</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Alibaba releases open-source AI-powered CLI tool for automated code review, demonstrating practical applications of LLMs in development workflows.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Alibaba</a> | 2026-06-05\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Coding</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Code Review</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/quantization-aware-training-gemma-4/\">Gemma 4 QAT models</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google releases Gemma 4 with Quantization-Aware Training (QAT) models, optimizing LLMs for efficient deployment on edge devices.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Google</a> | 2026-06-05\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Edge AI</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Google Gemma</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/05/the-token-bill-comes-due-inside-the-industry-scramble-to-manage-ais-runaway-costs/\">The token bill comes due</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        TechCrunch investigates how companies are struggling to manage spiraling AI infrastructure costs, with Uber implementing usage caps.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/\">Lorenzo Franceschi-Bicchierai</a> | 2026-06-05\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">TechCrunch</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Economics</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Enterprise AI</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM Pricing</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/institute/recursive-self-improvement\">When AI Builds Itself</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic publishes research on AI systems that can improve themselves, discussing progress toward recursive self-improvement capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Anthropic</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Research</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AGI</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/defending-code-reference-harness\">AI vulnerability discovery framework</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic releases 'defending-code-reference-harness', an open-source framework using AI to discover security vulnerabilities in code.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Anthropic</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Security</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Code Review</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://kasra.blog/blog/i-spent-1500-seeing-if-llms-could-hack-my-app/\">Testing LLMs for vulnerability discovery</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Security researcher creates intentionally vulnerable application and tests multiple LLMs' ability to identify and exploit security vulnerabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Kasra</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Security</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM Hacking</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Security</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://maxleiter.com/blog/weights\">They're made out of weights</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Deep exploration of how LLMs and AI models fundamentally work at the weight level, discussing neural networks and model architectures.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Max Leiter</a> | 2026-06-03\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Neural Networks</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/3/uber-caps-usage/\">Uber Caps Usage of AI Tools Like Claude Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Uber implements usage caps on AI coding tools like Claude Code to manage costs, highlighting economic realities of AI tool adoption at scale.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-06-03\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Economics</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Coding Agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Enterprise AI</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/2/microsofts-new-models/\">Microsoft's New Models</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison analyzes Microsoft's latest LLM release, focusing on training data implications and model quality considerations.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-06-02\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Microsoft</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Training Data</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-discussion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48406174\">Ask HN: What was your 'oh shit' moment with GenAI?</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Hacker News community discussion sharing surprising, concerning, or breakthrough moments with generative AI tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">HN Community</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">GenAI</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Community</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Experiences</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-discussion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://www.dailycal.org/news/campus/academics/failing-grades-soar-as-professors-see-greater-ai-usage-dwindling-math-skills-in-uc-berkeley/article_16fad0bf-02cb-4b8c-8d88-888ffd9f8608.html\">Failing grades soar with AI usage</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        UC Berkeley reports significant increase in failing grades correlated with AI tool usage, raising concerns about foundational skills erosion.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Daily Cal</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Education</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Academic Integrity</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-discussion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://www.buchodi.com/meta-glasses-facial-recognition/\">Meta's ships facial recognition on smart glasses</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Meta launches facial recognition capabilities on their smart glasses, raising privacy and surveillance concerns about AI-powered hardware.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\">Buchodi</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">HN</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Hardware</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Facial Recognition</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Privacy</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/1/hackers-simply-asked-meta-ai/\">Hackers Asked Meta AI to Write Malicious Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Security researchers demonstrate how Meta AI can be manipulated to generate malicious code through prompt engineering, highlighting AI safety concerns.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-06-01\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Security</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Meta</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Prompt Injection</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/01/hackers-hijacked-instagram-accounts-by-tricking-meta-ai-support-chatbot-into-granting-access/\">Meta AI chatbot vulnerability</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Security researchers discovered that Meta's AI support chatbot could be tricked into granting unauthorized access to Instagram accounts.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/\">Lorenzo Franceschi-Bicchierai</a> | 2026-06-01\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">TechCrunch</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Security</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Meta</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Social Engineering</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/andreas-kling/\">Andreas Kling on Ladybird Development</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Andreas Kling discusses development philosophy changes for the Ladybird browser project, with commentary on AI ethics and open-source development.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-06-05\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Open Source</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Ethics</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Browser Development</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/a-slightly-different-version/\">Google's AI Statement Changes</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        404 Media reports that Google asked to change their statement, removing the phrase about keeping humans in the loop, raising oversight concerns.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        By <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Simon Willison</a> | 2026-06-04\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Ethics</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Google</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI Oversight</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <a href=\"#\">Previous Reports</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Methodology</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n            <span>|</span>\n            <span>Generated with Claude Code</span>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
