                            <span class=\"topic\">AI Education</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic\">Academic Integrity</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/3/uber-caps-usage/\">Uber Caps Usage of AI Tools Like Claude Code to Manage Costs</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"author\">\n                            <span>By Simon Willison</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge blog\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"description\">Uber implements usage caps on AI coding tools like Claude Code to manage costs, highlighting the economic realities of AI tool adoption at scale.</div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic\">AI Economics</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic\">Coding Agents</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://maxleiter.com/blog/weights\">They're made out of weights</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"author\">\n                            <span>By Max Leiter</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge hn\">HN</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"description\">Deep exploration of how LLMs and AI models fundamentally work at the weight level, discussing the nature of neural networks and model architectures.</div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic\">Neural Networks</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/2/microsofts-new-models/\">Microsoft's New Models (Training Data Implications)</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"author\">\n                            <span>By Simon Willison</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge blog\">Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"description\">Simon Willison analyzes Microsoft's latest LLM release, focusing on training data implications and model quality considerations.</div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic\">Microsoft</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/01/hackers-hijacked-instagram-accounts-by-tricking-meta-ai-support-chatbot-into-granting-access/\">Hackers hijacked Instagram accounts by tricking Meta AI support chatbot into granting access</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"author\">\n                            <span>By Lorenzo Franceschi-Bicchierai</span>\n                            <span class=\"source-badge techcrunch\">TechCrunch</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"description\">Security researchers discovered that Meta's AI support chatbot could be tricked into granting unauthorized access to Instagram accounts through social engineering.</div>\n                        <div class=\"topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic\">AI Security</sp